=== AC5 — prevention proof (the real regression test) ===
Pre-check: grep -c "ConversationController" vendor/composer/autoload_classmap.php -> 0
(App\ namespace is PSR-4-resolved at runtime, not classmap-snapshotted — this is the
self-healing property the fix restores for local/dev.)

Ran, from the worktree:
  $ composer install --no-interaction
  Nothing to install, update or remove
  Generating autoload files ... (package:discover) ... done

NO manual `composer dump-autoload` was run afterward. Immediately after, with zero delay:
  GET /api/v1/delivery-man/message/list?token=<ali>                      -> HTTP 200
  GET /api/v1/delivery-man/message/search-list?token=<ali>&name=customer -> HTTP 200
  GET /api/v1/delivery-man/message/details?token=<ali>&conversation_id=60 -> HTTP 200
Post-install classmap re-check: grep -c "ConversationController" vendor/composer/autoload_classmap.php -> 0
laravel.log line count unchanged (1026 -> 1026) after this second round of hits — clean.

This directly reproduces the ticket's described regression scenario (a new PSR-4 class
landing without a manual dump-autoload) and confirms the endpoints resolve on the first
try post-install, independently re-confirming the engineer's own build-time verification.

